Subject: [PATCH 0020] Prism: spaces dashboard as a window-level mode

Recon §8: ego's spaces dashboard is a native overlay mode of the browser
window, not a tab. SetSpacesModeActive() switches the whole window:
- the toolbar row, bookmark bar, and infobar container collapse
  (visibility-gated layout via IsToolbarVisible / IsBookmarkBarVisible /
  IsInfobarVisible); TopContainerView's children and the Reload menu
  button hide individually so no control lingers in the macOS
  accessibility tree;
- the tab strip row reduces to the mode bar: native "N Spaces ⌄" caption
  centered at tab-strip height (PrismSpacesCaptionButton, overlay) + the
  corner spaces trigger (patch 0019) — tabs and all other buttons hide;
- the spaces wall (PrismSpacesModeHost, overlay: a views::WebView hosting
  chrome://prism-spaces?window=1) fills the client area edge to edge,
  laid out in BrowserView::Layout below the tab-strip row. The contents
  container's children hide and the active tab is WasHidden/WasShown, so
  the covered page leaves the accessibility tree (the container itself
  must stay visible — the tabbed layout CHECKs it).

No dashboard tab ever exists; ⌥S / corner trigger / agent menu toggle the
mode; choosing a card or a caption item exits into that space
(focus + show completion matches the wall's own exit action).
